 Architecture, development, backups, API, and security notes are in [architecture.md](architecture.md).
+
+## Android install and reminders
+
+1. Serve the app over HTTPS (required for install and push).
+2. Open it in Chrome on Android, then **⋮ → Install app** (or Add to Home screen).
+3. Tap the bell icon in the header and choose **Enable reminders**; allow notifications.
+4. When adding or editing a task, set a **Reminder time** and how long before to be notified.
+
+Reminders are Web Push messages sent by the server, so they arrive when the app is closed. VAPID keys are generated on first start and stored in the SQLite database; keep the data volume so existing subscriptions stay valid. The reminder clock uses the time zone your phone last reported. Set `VAPID_SUBJECT` in `.env` if you want a contact address in push requests.
